{# Traffic Scotland incident notice (19 Nov 2026). Rendered only when
   THIS build read Traffic Scotland's Unplanned Events feed AND it holds a
   live event on the A78 (Ardrossan to Greenock) or the A737 (Dalry to
   Johnstone) -- see loadTrunk in scripts/fetch-data.mjs. On a failed
   fetch there is no notice: a closure that may have cleared must not
   stand on the front page. When Traffic Scotland drops the event
   the notice goes.

   A QUIET DAY (21 Nov 2026, Ian). "Is the road open?" is the commonest
   search that reaches this site, and an empty page does not answer it.
   So where every event is shown (`trunkAll`) and the page also carries
   the road camera, a feed read by THIS build with nothing for our roads
   is reported as exactly that: what Traffic Scotland is reporting, on
   which stretches, when it was checked, and that the Haylie Brae road is
   not covered. It is hidden by the reader's browser after 40 minutes,
   and never shown after a failed fetch. The front page stays silent.

   The sentence is Traffic Scotland's, unedited. The site adds the badge,
   the time and, for the A737, the words that say which road that is to a
   Largs reader. Red for a closure, amber for anything less; the badge
   says so in words as well, so the colour is never the only signal.

   The front page shows the most serious event and counts the rest. A page
   that sets `trunkAll` before the include (Roadworks) shows every one.
   Same frame as the power-cut and flood notices. #}
{# 25 Nov 2026: a closure that is the planned one (planned.json, `match`)
   is reported inside planned-notice.njk, so it is left out here. Everything
   else Traffic Scotland reports is shown exactly as before. #}
{% set trunkPlannedNow = planned.closures | currentNotices %}
{% set trunkKept = [] %}
{% if today.trunk and today.trunk.ok %}{% for t in today.trunk.items %}{% set trunkHit = [] %}{% if t.closed %}{% for c in trunkPlannedNow %}{% for w in (c.match or []) %}{% if (w | lower) in (t.text | lower) %}{% set trunkHit = (trunkHit.push(1), trunkHit) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% if not (trunkHit | length) %}{% set trunkKept = (trunkKept.push(t), trunkKept) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if today.trunk and today.trunk.ok and trunkKept | length %}
{% set trunkShown = trunkKept if trunkAll else [trunkKept[0]] %}
{% set trunkMore = (trunkKept | length) - (trunkShown | length) %}
<div class="wrap">
  {% for t in trunkShown %}
  <div class="power-notice trunk-notice{% if not t.closed %} trunk-incident{% endif %}" role="status">
    <span class="power-notice-badge">{{ t.badge }}</span>
    <span class="power-notice-text">
      {% if t.lead %}<strong>{{ t.lead }}</strong> — {% endif %}{{ t.text }}{% if t.whenValue %} · {{ t.whenLabel }} <span class="mono">{{ t.whenValue }}</span>{% endif %}{% if trunkMore > 0 %} · <a href="/roadworks/">and {{ trunkMore }} more →</a>{% endif %} · <a href="https://www.traffic.gov.scot/traffic-information/incidents">Traffic Scotland →</a>
    </span>
    <span class="power-notice-src">Traffic Scotland · checked {{ today.trunk.checkedAt | hhmm }}</span>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% elif trunkAll and today.trunk and today.trunk.ok and view and (view.key == "all" or isRoute) %}
<div class="wrap">
  <p class="trunk-clear" role="status" data-checked="{{ today.trunk.checkedAt }}">
    {# 25 Nov 2026: with a planned closure live (planned.json), "no
       closures" read as a contradiction of the notice above it. The feed
       is unplanned events only, so say that, and say the planned one is
       not in it. #}
    {% set trunkPlanned = planned.closures | currentNotices %}
    {% if trunkPlanned | length %}Apart from the planned closure above, Traffic Scotland is reporting <strong>no incidents</strong> on{% else %}Traffic Scotland is reporting <strong>no closures or incidents</strong> on{% endif %}
    the A78 between Ardrossan and Greenock, or on the A737 between Dalry and
    Johnstone <span class="trunk-clear-src">· checked <span class="mono">{{ today.trunk.checkedAt | hhmm }}</span></span>.
    {% if trunkPlanned | length %}Its feed carries unplanned events only. {% endif %}It does not cover the Haylie Brae road (A760): see the road camera below.
  </p>
</div>
<script>
(function () {
  var el = document.querySelector(".trunk-clear[data-checked]");
  if (!el) return;
  var at = Date.parse(el.getAttribute("data-checked"));
  if (!at) return;
  function tick() { if ((Date.now() - at) / 60000 > 40) el.hidden = true; }
  tick();
  setInterval(tick, 60000);
})();
</script>
{% endif %}
